---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the astro-seo-enforcer demo and its checks"
  description="Why this demo exists, what each route proves about the integration, and how a single failed rule turns the local build and the CI pipeline red."
>
  <h1>About this demo</h1>
  <p>
    This is a second route, so the duplicate-title rule has something real to
    compare against. Its title and description differ from every other page here.
  </p>
  <h2>How the check runs</h2>
  <p>
    After Astro writes the static files, the integration walks the output
    directory, parses each HTML document once and runs the enabled rules against
    it. Titles are also collected globally to detect duplicates across pages.
  </p>
  <h3>Failure behaviour</h3>
  <p>
    On a violation the build prints a grouped, readable report and exits with a
    non-zero status code. Return to the <a href="/">demo home page</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
